<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="1dc0d977">In contrast to the more formal and detailed architecture diagrams, the architecture overview is a high-level
sketch of the architecture.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The diagram generally shows the components of an architecture including, but not limited to, major systems,
interconnections, and actors along with high level supporting information such as relationships between different
components (for example association, composition, and aggregation). &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
This diagram may embody key objectives, requirements, and constraints for the engagement and highlight work areas to be
investigated in more detail with formal architecture modeling.&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="84cf0164"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="9f808922"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="7d4062a6"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="f1a5a91">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of this artifact is to:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Quickly onboard stakeholders with an executive level viewpoint of components necessary to build a solution/s that
        solve the future state business need.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Provide high level guidance around the structure, components, and scope of the architecture to developers 
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Create early opportunities for stakeholders to identify any impacts of the architecture and enable timely
        resolution
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="be9516e2"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="88879e5c"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="f0902e36">&lt;p&gt;
    May be developed in a form of one pager or a few pages document that is concise and provides an understanding of a
    target architecture on a high level.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
